      "writtenOn": "2020-08-12T05:20:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "d_path() is used for SecureOS Kernel driver. Secure OS\u0027s Application using GP(Global Platform) API needs to distinguish client Application. And SecureOS kernel driver get client application path using d_path() and make hash value using the path information to distinguish Client Application.\nd_path() is used only to get file path information and not used any other purpose. So, I\u0027m not sure why this function cannot be allowed to Kernel Module.. :(\nCould you allow to use this function for this SecureOS kernel driver\u0027s purpose? Or If we cannot use the function, could you recommend alternative function for our purpose?",
      "parentUuid": "3a9d8384_f308a553",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 360,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 360,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "581cf45e3dc2dd16dc74a551300b6436c6f5b011",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
